1
00:00:03,211 --> 00:00:07,778
Cyber Monday is the one night a retail team runs dozens of deals

2
00:00:07,778 --> 00:00:11,631
at once, so I drew the deal desk as a midnight arcade.

3
00:00:12,081 --> 00:00:15,978
Every deal is a shop window that glows brighter as it sells,

4
00:00:15,978 --> 00:00:19,421
with a queue outside sized by the last hour of sales.

5
00:00:20,479 --> 00:00:23,721
This TV sold out before dawn, so its window is dark

6
00:00:23,721 --> 00:00:26,899
under a sold-out sign and the queue has gone home.

7
00:00:27,349 --> 00:00:30,762
An amber shutter means a deal will sell out before

8
00:00:30,762 --> 00:00:34,039
it ends, and the time is written on the shutter.

9
00:00:34,845 --> 00:00:38,940
Switch the lens to sell-out risk and every window is lit by

10
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:43,105
whether it runs out early, misses its target or is on track.

11
00:00:43,909 --> 00:00:48,740
Today ranks what needs me: the earbuds run out within two hours, two

12
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:54,139
deep discounts wait for approval, and one draft sits below the margin floor.

13
00:00:54,945 --> 00:00:58,900
The clock across the top replays the day from the sales, so

14
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:02,385
I can watch each window light up and the TV go dark.

15
00:01:06,121 --> 00:01:09,390
Viewed as an approver, everything that is not

16
00:01:09,390 --> 00:01:12,151
waiting at the velvet rope steps back.

17
00:01:12,957 --> 00:01:18,340
In the Shopfront the margin guard checks the price as I type: at forty-six dollars this

18
00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:23,847
racer makes four point three percent, under the eight percent floor, so it will not save.

19
00:01:24,297 --> 00:01:29,957
At fifty-two dollars the margin clears the floor, but forty-seven percent off is

20
00:01:29,957 --> 00:01:34,627
a deep discount, so it goes to the velvet rope instead of opening.

21
00:01:35,556 --> 00:01:37,911
I set that price, so the rope will

22
00:01:37,911 --> 00:01:40,266
not open for me, even as an admin.

23
00:01:40,716 --> 00:01:44,145
Jordan approves it from the same queue, and the approval

24
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:47,146
is its own record that the owner can never write.

25
00:01:47,948 --> 00:01:52,473
The Ticker shows the numbers behind the amber shutter: at forty units

26
00:01:52,473 --> 00:01:56,998
an hour, the last earbuds go mid-morning, hours before the deal ends.

27
00:01:57,809 --> 00:02:01,384
Doorbuster: no deal below cost, no deep discount without

28
00:02:01,384 --> 00:02:04,639
a second person, and no sell-out nobody saw coming.
